      "situation": "The bank's payments journey has recovered. The recovery check passed: the last two looks in a row were clean, the last at 49 s.",
      "background": "The pipeline changed payments max_transfer_minor from 1000000 to 1, and payments began rejecting transfers as over the limit. Around the same time, the clearing process exited (exit code 15), and the screening primary slowed to a p95 of 1823 ms against a 15 ms baseline, timing out every call.",
      "assessment": "The incident commander reverted payments max_transfer_minor to 1000000, which cleared the '422 amount exceeds transfer limit' rejections. It restarted clearing, which has stayed up since, and failed screening over to screening-standby (release 4.1, restarted earlier by ops-maintenance), which cleared the 503s.",
      "recommendation": "Find out why the pipeline set max_transfer_minor to 1 and why clearing was terminated, and repair the slow screening primary before failing back from screening-standby. Operations should review the payments wrongly rejected while the limit was 1, and those that failed with 503 during the screening timeouts, so customers can retry or be told."
    },
